def H(code, d, q, right, wrong, e): return B.hand(code, d, q, right, wrong, e)
H("886.d.1.A",3,"Two interns compare how business greetings, gift giving and meeting times differ in Japan and Brazil. They are:","identifying similarities and differences in international cultures",["ignoring culture","assuming all cultures match","skipping research"],"Cultural comparison.")
H("886.d.1.A",4,"Before a partner visit from another country, a logistics firm studies local customs mainly to:","avoid misunderstandings and build trust",["avoid the visit","save money on lunch","shorten the contract"],"Cultural awareness.")
H("886.d.1.B",3,"A trainee lists the largest ports, rail hubs and consumer markets in Asia, Europe and the Americas. She is explaining:","the variety of world markets",["a single market","no markets","local shops only"],"World markets.")
H("886.d.1.B",4,"Emerging markets are of interest to distributors because they often show:","fast growth and rising consumer demand",["no demand","no growth","no trade"],"Market growth.")
H("886.d.1.C",3,"A shipper changes the packaging colors and language on a product for a new foreign market after learning local preferences. This shows:","marketing factors and practices that impact other cultures",["ignoring culture","one design for all","no research"],"Adapt marketing.")
H("886.d.1.C",4,"A product name that sounds fine in English but has a poor meaning abroad shows why firms must:","research language and culture before launching",["skip research","ignore feedback","avoid exporting"],"Localize.")
H("886.d.2.A",3,"A student writes a glossary with 'freight', 'warehousing', 'cross-docking' and 'inventory turnover'. She is:","defining terms associated with the distribution and logistics industries",["avoiding terms","guessing meanings","skipping vocabulary"],"Vocabulary.")
H("886.d.2.A",4,"Cross-docking is a practice in which goods are:","moved from inbound to outbound trucks with little or no storage",["stored for months","destroyed","painted"],"Cross-dock.")
H("886.d.2.B",3,"A career fair handout explains that distribution and logistics includes trucking, warehousing, air cargo, rail and freight forwarding. It is identifying:","the scope of the distribution and logistics industries and industry sectors",["one narrow job","no sectors","only retail"],"Scope.")
H("886.d.2.B",4,"A freight forwarder is a business that:","arranges shipments between shippers and carriers",["builds roads","makes trucks","prints maps"],"Freight forwarder.")
H("886.d.2.C",3,"A class reads about the rise of containerized shipping and the recent growth of same-day delivery. They are identifying:","significant historical and current issues in the distribution and logistics industries",["no issues","only old news","only fiction"],"History and current issues.")
H("886.d.2.C",4,"Container shipping changed global trade mainly by:","standardizing loads so cargo moves faster between ships, trains and trucks",["slowing ports","ending shipping","shrinking boats"],"Containerization.")
H("886.d.2.D",3,"A planner sketches how drones, autonomous trucks and robotic warehouses could reshape delivery in ten years. She is identifying:","potential future scenarios for the distribution and logistics industries",["the distant past","nothing","a recipe"],"Future scenarios.")
H("886.d.2.D",4,"A likely future trend in warehouses is:","more automation and robotic picking",["fewer computers","no inventory","no workers ever"],"Automation.")
H("886.d.2.E",3,"A company adds tracking sensors to containers and expands to overseas suppliers. This shows how:","emerging technology and globalization impact the distribution and logistics industries",["nothing changes","technology is irrelevant","trade is shrinking"],"Tech and globalization.")
H("886.d.2.E",4,"One effect of globalization on logistics is:","longer supply chains that need more coordination",["shorter supply chains only","less shipping","no trade"],"Longer chains.")
H("886.d.2.F",3,"Students compare driver shortages in trucking with port congestion in ocean shipping. They are:","comparing and contrasting issues affecting the distribution and logistics industries",["ignoring issues","describing one issue only","writing a story"],"Compare issues.")
H("886.d.2.F",4,"Port congestion differs from driver shortages in that congestion mainly delays:","cargo waiting at terminals, while shortages limit trucks available to move it",["nothing","paint drying","school buses"],"Different bottlenecks.")
H("886.d.3.A",3,"A class studies why nations trade: resources one country lacks, cheaper production elsewhere and larger markets. They are identifying:","reasons for world trade and globalization",["reasons to avoid trade","a single reason","no reasons"],"Why trade.")
H("886.d.3.A",4,"Comparative advantage explains why countries trade because they:","specialize in what they produce relatively best",["produce everything","never trade","only import"],"Specialization.")
H("886.d.3.B",3,"A report explains how a port strike, a trade war or a sanction can change what stores can stock. This is identifying:","the political impact of distribution and logistics",["no politics","no impact","only weather"],"Political impact.")
H("886.d.3.B",4,"Trade sanctions affect logistics firms by:","limiting what and where they may ship",["lowering all prices","opening all ports","removing paperwork"],"Sanctions.")
H("886.d.3.C",3,"A compliance officer reviews labor, safety and customs laws to see how they affect warehouse operations and shipping routes. She is:","reviewing regulations and major laws to evaluate their impact on the industry",["ignoring laws","breaking laws","guessing"],"Review laws.")
H("886.d.3.C",4,"A company that fails to follow cargo regulations risks:","fines, delays and loss of shipping privileges",["a bonus","free freight","faster customs"],"Compliance risk.")
H("886.d.3.D",3,"Each morning a supply-chain analyst reads trade journals and freight news to learn about delays and rate changes. She is:","reading written material to stay abreast of current issues",["ignoring news","avoiding reading","only watching TV"],"Stay informed.")
H("886.d.3.D",4,"Staying current with industry news helps a logistics planner:","anticipate disruptions and adjust plans",["miss changes","ignore risk","slow work"],"Anticipate.")
H("886.d.3.E",3,"Faced with a closed bridge, a dispatcher lists three alternate routes, compares time and cost and picks the best. She is using:","critical-thinking skills to identify and organize alternatives and evaluate options",["no thinking","a coin flip","guessing"],"Critical thinking.")
H("886.d.3.E",4,"The best way to compare alternatives is to:","list the options and weigh each against cost, time and risk",["pick the first","ignore costs","choose randomly"],"Evaluate options.")
H("886.d.3.F",3,"A manager reviews on-time delivery rates and checks that a hired trucking contractor meets the terms of its contract. She is:","evaluating performance and contract compliance of contractors and service providers",["ignoring contracts","skipping reviews","guessing"],"Contract compliance.")
H("886.d.3.F",4,"A contractor who repeatedly misses delivery windows should:","be addressed using contract terms and possibly replaced",["be ignored","be rewarded","be given more loads"],"Enforce the contract.")
H("886.d.4.A",3,"A clerk finds a pricing error in the shop's favor and reports it to a manager instead of keeping quiet. This shows:","workplace ethical and legal responsibilities",["dishonesty","ignoring rules","a legal shortcut"],"Ethics.")
H("886.d.4.A",4,"Accepting a gift from a supplier in exchange for a contract could be:","an ethics and legal violation",["acceptable","required","encouraged"],"Conflict of interest.")
H("886.d.4.B",3,"A new hire greets customers politely, silences his phone in meetings and thanks coworkers. He is:","using proper etiquette and behavior",["being rude","ignoring others","interrupting"],"Etiquette.")
H("886.d.4.B",4,"Good workplace etiquette includes:","respecting others' time and personal space",["interrupting","gossiping","arriving late"],"Respect.")
H("886.d.4.C",3,"A warehouse supervisor expects clean uniforms, closed-toe boots, hair tied back near machines and good hygiene. She is identifying:","appropriate personal appearance and health habits",["no standards","any outfit","skipping safety"],"Appearance and health.")
H("886.d.4.C",4,"Hair tied back and no loose jewelry near conveyors helps:","prevent entanglement injuries",["cause injuries","slow work","look worse"],"Safety appearance.")
H("886.d.4.D",3,"A dispatcher repeats a driver's problem back, asks questions and then writes a short email summarizing the plan. She is:","practicing written and oral communication and effective listening",["ignoring the driver","guessing","avoiding contact"],"Listening and writing.")
H("886.d.4.D",4,"A driver explains a late load, and the dispatcher nods, asks a clarifying question and restates the problem. That is an example of:","active listening, which means paying attention and summarizing what was said",["interrupting to give orders","looking at a phone while he talks","tuning out until he finishes"],"Active listening.")
H("886.d.4.E",3,"A student reads a technical manual on pallet racking load limits and explains it in her own words. She is:","comprehending technical reading materials common to the distribution and logistics industries",["avoiding reading","guessing","skipping manuals"],"Technical reading.")
H("886.d.4.E",4,"A rated load limit on a rack means:","the maximum weight the rack can safely hold",["the minimum weight","the paint amount","the price"],"Load rating.")
H("886.d.4.F",3,"Before a presentation on dock safety, Eli outlines his points, rehearses and practices short answers for questions he might get. He is:","employing sound writing and preparation skills for prepared and extemporaneous oral presentations",["not preparing","reading blindly","avoiding practice"],"Prepare to speak.")
H("886.d.4.F",4,"An extemporaneous speech differs from a prepared speech because it is:","given with little or no advance preparation",["written word for word","memorized exactly","read from a script"],"Extemporaneous.")
H("886.d.4.G",3,"During a team huddle, a lead speaks clearly, makes eye contact and uses a steady pace. She is demonstrating:","speaking skills",["poor speaking","whispering","mumbling"],"Speaking skills.")
H("886.d.4.G",4,"Good speakers keep an audience engaged by:","using eye contact, clear volume and a steady pace",["reading from slides","staring at the floor","speaking too fast"],"Engagement.")
H("886.d.5.A",3,"A student lists areas where research and development happens, such as new packaging materials, safer forklifts and route-planning software. She is:","defining major fields of research and development",["avoiding research","naming one field only","guessing"],"R&D fields.")
H("886.d.5.A",4,"Research and development in logistics often aims to:","improve efficiency, safety or cost",["raise costs","slow deliveries","avoid change"],"R&D goals.")
H("886.d.5.B",3,"A researcher uses trade journals, industry databases and interviews with warehouse managers to study new tracking tools. She is:","demonstrating proficiency in using a variety of resources for research and development",["using one resource","guessing","skipping research"],"Use varied resources.")
H("886.d.5.B",4,"Using several sources in research helps a student:","confirm facts and see different viewpoints",["avoid checking","limit ideas","hide errors"],"Multiple sources.")
H("886.d.5.C",3,"A team tests whether a new packing method reduces damage by running trials, recording results and comparing them to a control. They are describing:","the scientific method of research",["a random guess","a rumor","an opinion"],"Scientific method.")
H("886.d.5.C",4,"In the scientific method, a hypothesis is:","a testable prediction",["a final result","a proven law","a survey"],"Hypothesis.")
H("886.d.6.A",3,"A team writes up a plan to pilot barcode scanning at one dock, stating its goal, budget and schedule. They are:","discussing project proposals",["skipping planning","avoiding goals","guessing"],"Project proposal.")
H("886.d.6.A",4,"Before the dock team can get approval to try new scanners, the proposal must spell out:","the project goal, the timeline and the budget",["a joke and a menu","only a map of the lot","only the crew's favorite colors"],"Proposal parts.")
H("886.d.6.B",3,"A student keeps a log of each shipment she handles, with dates, quantities and signatures. She is:","developing and maintaining records",["avoiding records","tossing papers","ignoring logs"],"Records.")
H("886.d.6.B",4,"Accurate shipping records are valuable because they:","help resolve disputes and track performance",["cause disputes","hide errors","slow work"],"Record value.")
H("886.d.6.C",3,"A clerk records weekly pallet counts and turns the numbers into a bar chart. She is:","collecting and organizing data in graphs, tables, charts and plots",["avoiding data","guessing","ignoring numbers"],"Organize data.")
H("886.d.6.C",4,"Hana wants a chart showing how weekly damaged-carton counts rose and fell over six months. The best choice is:","a line graph, which shows change over time",["a pie chart of names","a map of the lot","a list of drivers"],"Line graph.")
H("886.d.6.D",3,"A manager reads a chart showing late deliveries rise every Friday and concludes staffing is thin that day. She is:","analyzing and interpreting data from graphs, tables, charts and plots",["ignoring the chart","guessing","misreading data"],"Interpret data.")
H("886.d.6.D",4,"A rising trend on a chart of damage claims suggests:","a growing problem that needs investigating",["no problem","a perfect year","fewer claims"],"Read the trend.")
H("886.d.6.E",3,"The warehouse keeps a journal of purchases, an inventory count and an income statement for the year. This is:","maintaining appropriate financial records such as journals, inventories and income statements",["no records","random lists","a budget only"],"Financial records.")
H("886.d.6.E",4,"An income statement shows a company's:","revenue, expenses and profit over a period",["employee names","truck colors","delivery routes"],"Income statement.")
H("886.d.6.F",3,"At the end of a project, a class checks whether it hit its objectives and whether it stayed in budget. They are:","conducting formative, summative and financial analyses of project learning objectives",["skipping evaluation","guessing","ignoring results"],"Project evaluation.")
H("886.d.6.F",4,"A summative analysis is done:","at the end to judge overall results",["at the start","never","only during lunch"],"Summative.")
